Cook ground chuck and onion in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat until browned, stirring to crumbe.  Drain and pat dry with paper towels. Drain and pat dry with paper towels.  Return meat to skillet; stir in tomato sauce and seasonings. Continue to cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, until throughtly heated.  Layer tortillas, meat sauce, and cheese in a 2 quart casserole dish coated with cooking spray; pour water over top.  Cover and bake at 400 degrees fro 20 minutes. Serve hot. Food Exchange per serving: 2 MEDIUM-FAT MEATS EXCHANGE + 1 VEGETABLE EXCHANGE; CAL: 157; CAR: 6gm; PRO: 16gm; FAT: 7gm; SOD: 429;

Source: The ALL NEW Cookbook for Diabetics and Their Families by WHOM

